34,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I learned a lot! It turns out transport is a huge part of the budget, and those whole-building lets can be really risky if people drop out at the last minute.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I see. I've discovered that the evenings are where the real bonding happens, but sadly, many members have stopped attending the away camps altogether.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are concerning. The public booking process is a bureaucratic nightmare, and relying on the campus canteen is impossible since it closes, meaning we'd be stuck with heavy cooking duties.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that the public beds are cheap, but the inland centers are a nightmare! Eight people to a room and strict lights-out? No wonder everyone was so tired last time!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The local option is also problematic. The hall is already crowded with other clubs, and a third of our members can't even make it to campus by nine without staying overnight.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"That's a lot of problems! If transport is so expensive and whole-building lets are risky, maybe we should look for something that balances cost and stability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is heartbreaking to think that we are losing members because they don't feel connected. If we want them to stay, we must find a way to ensure everyone sleeps and socializes together.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we want to avoid burnout, we can't choose a place that requires a nine-page application or forces us to spend hours cooking every day. We need a streamlined process.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"I'm with Ryuji! If we're crammed eight to a room with a strict curfew, we'll be just as exhausted as last year. We need a place where we can actually rest!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"It seems every option has a significant drawback. If the local hall is overbooked and the commute is a barrier, staying on campus isn't a simple fix.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,Maybe we should consider a place that handles the meals for us? That would solve Ryuji's cooking problem and might make the experience more relaxing for everyone.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"That would be lovely, Mio. If the meals are provided, it would leave us more time to focus on the members and encourage those who have felt distant to rejoin us.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A place with staff for meals would certainly reduce the burden on the organizers, but we must be careful about the booking process and the overall cost.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I just want to make sure we aren't trading cooking duties for zero sleep! If we go somewhere with staff, I hope the rooms are actually decent.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we prioritize meal services and ease of booking, we have to be very careful about the final cost per person to avoid any budget deficits.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm starting to think we need to be really careful about how we structure the payment, especially if we go for a place with a fixed headcount.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Mio. We must ensure that the financial arrangements are fair and transparent so that no one feels excluded or stressed by the cost.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We need to weigh the administrative ease against the potential for member burnout. If the booking is too complex or the duties too heavy, the camp fails before it starts.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just want a place where we can actually sleep and not be treated like we're in a boot camp! If the inland places are that bad, we have to look elsewhere.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Let's keep our eyes on the total cost. We can't afford another deficit, so we need to be realistic about what we can actually commit to.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
